{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00647",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 13.42,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "Hello! I'm so sorry to be back, I feel like I'm wasting your time, but this throat just won't go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.99,
      "end_seconds": 24.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Not wasting it at all. When did it start, and what's happened since? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.47,
      "end_seconds": 45.96,
      "duration_seconds": 20.49,
      "text": "Nine days ago, and it started with a scratchy bit, and then it got worse and I couldn't swallow properly, so I went to the pharmacy and they gave me a course of something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.35,
      "end_seconds": 52.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Do you know what it was? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.41,
      "end_seconds": 72.22,
      "duration_seconds": 16.81,
      "text": "A course, antibiotics I think, I finished it yesterday, and I thought it'd be gone, but it's not, it's actually worse, my left ear hurts when I swallow too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.53,
      "end_seconds": 84.27,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "So you've had a sore throat for nine days and it's not improving. How would you rate the pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.29,
      "end_seconds": 91.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "It's bad. I'd say severe at the moment. I can't eat toast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.42,
      "end_seconds": 93.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.89,
      "end_seconds": 102.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "No, no fever, I've been taking my temperature. It's been normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.21,
      "end_seconds": 110.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies, particularly to antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.2,
      "end_seconds": 126.73,
      "duration_seconds": 13.53,
      "text": "Penicillin, I believe. I know I react to it, but I honestly can't remember what happened. It was years ago and Mum told me not to take it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.95,
      "end_seconds": 136.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "That's very useful, so we'll avoid that whole family. Anything else in your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.99,
      "end_seconds": 141.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Just asthma, but it's mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.29,
      "end_seconds": 149.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Okay. Let's look at your throat. Open wide and say ahh. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.83,
      "end_seconds": 163.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Ahhh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.93,
      "end_seconds": 174.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "Your tonsils are red and swollen, and there are white patches on both of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.49,
      "end_seconds": 178.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Is that bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.52,
      "end_seconds": 192.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "It tells me there's a bacterial infection on the tonsils. It fits with tonsillitis, so I'd say bacterial tonsillitis is the likely cause."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.66,
      "end_seconds": 198.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "But I took the antibiotics. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.83,
      "end_seconds": 213.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "The pharmacy course may have been the wrong type or too short. And in your case, some of the commonest ones are the ones you can't take. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.7,
      "end_seconds": 217.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Right, because of the penicillin. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.11,
      "end_seconds": 228.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "Exactly. So I'm going to start you on clarithromycin, 500 mg twice a day, for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.71,
      "end_seconds": 233.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Is that different? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.96,
      "end_seconds": 247.81,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "It's a different family, which you can take safely with your penicillin reaction. It's for the throat infection, and take it with food."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.63,
      "end_seconds": 254.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else I should do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.21,
      "end_seconds": 265.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "Plenty of fluids, soft food, and rest. Gargling with warm salty water can ease the soreness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.88,
      "end_seconds": 269.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "I like a gargle. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.04,
      "end_seconds": 279.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "You should notice a difference after two days. If you don't, come back. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.77,
      "end_seconds": 286.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Will I need to come back anyway? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.0,
      "end_seconds": 300.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.86,
      "text": "Yes, I'd like to see you in a week to be sure it's gone, especially with the ear pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.2,
      "end_seconds": 307.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "A week. Perfect. Thank you so much. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.29,
      "end_seconds": 310.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Look after yourself. ~"
    }
  ]
}
